ruleGlobalT -- F-133: A RULE ACTION READS A DECLARED GLOBAL, AND THE GLOBAL SURVIVES THE FIRE.

processAction's labelToLocals loop, on a rule's fire, cleared every attribute of the rule's code that the label
did not carry. The code's attributes include the globals the body names, and they SHARE the global's body, so the
clear wiped the global itself: rgIn and rgMark read their tags, and rgFires restarted every fire. The gate
(GroupActions.rtn, rulesOwnOnly) clears only the rule's own locals and terms.

  RG-1  in-rule read of the global        want 987654
  RG-2  the global after two fires         want 987654
  RG-3  a global counter, two fires        want 2      (non-zero sibling: the global persists ACROSS fires)
  RG-4  fires that saw a stale local       want 0      (locals still clear per fire; regression guard only --
        the action loop below labelToLocals clears isLocal too, so this row cannot certify the gate, H17)

